{
  "title": "For All Market：Creator Outreach Quota Rule Adjustment",
  "content": "## 1. Background\nTargeted Collaboration is being upgraded so that invitation capacity follows **fit** rather than volume. Today a seller has one flat weekly outreach budget that can be spent on any creator. After the upgrade, capacity is allocated by **seller tier × creator level**, and sellers whose invitations actually convert into posts earn bonus capacity for higher-level creators.\n### 1.1 Old model vs new model\n| Dimension | Before | After (from Oct 15, 2026; subject to actual effective date) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Quota granularity | One shared weekly pool per shop | **One pool per creator level**, on top of the shop's total |\n| What limits a creator | Follower cap | Creator level, plus the remaining quota for that level |\n| Extra capacity | Aggregate bonus quota | Bonus quota **per level**, driven by exposure-to-post performance, **consumed first** |\n| Failure mode | Entire batch fails when the pool is empty | Only the exhausted level fails, returning **16024049** |\n| Pre-check | Remaining total = `quota_sum - quota_use` | Per-level remaining, plus a per-creator **eligibility check** |\n\n## 2. API changes\n**Compatibility**: no existing field, enum, or response shape is removed, and **no new permission scope** is introduced — already-authorized apps do not need re-authorization. The behavioral break is on the **invitation result**, not on the request contract: a request that was accepted before can now be rejected with `16024049`.\n\n### 2.1 Creator discovery gains creator_level\n| API | Change | Why it matters |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Seller Search Creator on Marketplace** <br> `POST /affiliate_seller/{202608\\|202508}/marketplace_creators/search` | New request parameter `creator_level` (`int64`) — filter candidates by creator level. <br> New response field `data.creators[].creator_level` (`int64`). | Candidate lists can be pulled level by level so a batch never mixes levels whose quotas differ. |\n| **Get Marketplace Creator Performance** <br> `GET /affiliate_seller/{202608\\|202508}/marketplace_creators/{creator_user_id}` | New response field `data.creator.creator_level` (`int64`). | Creator detail pages and CRM records can show the level that decides which quota bucket an invitation will hit. |\n### 2.2 Quota API returns per-level detail\n**Get Weekly Creator Outreach Quota** — `GET /affiliate_seller/202607/creator_outreach/quota`. All existing fields remain unchanged. A new `quota_detail` array is added to the response (if the shop has not been included in the rollout, this field returns empty).\n| New field | Type | Sample | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `quota_detail` | array<object> | — | Quota breakdown by creator level group. |\n| `quota_detail.creator_levels` | list | `[1,2,3]` | Creator levels this entry covers. |\n| `quota_detail.quota_period_sum` | int32 | 300 | Standard quota granted for the current period. |\n| `quota_detail.quota_period_use` | int32 | 100 | Standard quota already used. |\n| `quota_detail.quota_bonus_sum` | int32 | 100 | Bonus quota granted for the current period. |\n| `quota_detail.quota_bonus_use` | int32 | 100 | Bonus quota already used. |\n\n**Remaining capacity for a level group** = `(quota_bonus_sum - quota_bonus_use) + (quota_period_sum - quota_period_use)`. Bonus is consumed first, so tools that only track the standard numbers will under-count what the seller can still send.\n### 2.3 New API: Check Creator Outreach Eligibility\nA bulk pre-check for up to 100 candidates per call — determines whether each creator can be successfully invited and whether re-inviting is needed.\n#### API path\n| Item | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Method / path | `POST /affiliate/{version}/creator_outreach/eligibility/check` |\n#### Request parameters\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `creator_ids` | array<string> | Yes | List of candidate creator IDs. Recommended: 1–100 per call. |\n#### Response parameters\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `code` | integer | OpenAPI response status code. |\n| `message` | string | Response message. |\n| `request_id` | string | Request trace ID. |\n| `data` | object | Business response payload. |\n| `data.creator_quota_infos[]` | array<object> | Per-creator eligibility check results. |\n| ` .creator_id` | string | Creator ID. |\n| ` .is_connect` | boolean | Whether the creator is already connected with the seller. |\n| ` .is_paired` | boolean | Whether the creator is already paired with the seller. |\n| ` .is_blocked` | boolean | Whether the seller and creator have a mutual block. |\n| ` .block_types` | array<string> | Block types, if applicable. |\n| ` .is_conform_to_threshold` | boolean | Whether the creator meets the seller's outreach threshold. |\n| Response flag | How to use it |\n| --- | --- |\n| `is_blocked` / `block_types` | Drop the creator from the batch. Surface the reason in the UI instead of letting the invitation fail. |\n| `is_connect` / `is_paired` | Already connected or paired — route to the existing conversation rather than spending new quota. |\n| `is_conform_to_threshold` | **The key gate for this launch**: `false` means the creator sits above what this seller's tier can reach, so an invitation would be rejected. |\n### 2.4 New error: quota exhausted for a creator level\n| Code | Message | When it is returned |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **16024049** | `Outreach creator level has exceeded the quota limit.` | Invitation creation (**Create Target Collaboration**) when the target creator's level has no remaining standard or bonus quota. |\n\n**Do not blind-retry** **`16024049`**. Quota does not come back until the next Sunday refresh. Retrying burns rate limit and, in queue-based tools, can stall the rest of the batch. Re-read the quota, drop that level from the current run, and keep sending levels that still have capacity.\n\n\n## 3. Recommended integration flow\nThe shape of the change: quota checking moves from **one number before the batch** to **per-level remaining + per-creator eligibility check**.\n\n![Image](https://p16-arcosite-sg.ibyteimg.com/tos-alisg-i-k9wyc2ijk0-sg/054ee6af15ee400984c5217b4c27fb6d~tplv-k9wyc2ijk0-image.image)\n\n### 3.1 Step by step\n\n1. **Read the quota first.** Call **Get Weekly Creator Outreach Quota** once per planning run and cache `quota_detail` per level group together with `start_time` / `end_time`. Treat `unlimited=true` as \"no per-level cap\", but re-check it every period — allowlisted shops are moving off it.\n2. **Pull candidates by level.** Use the new `creator_level` filter in **Seller Search Creator on Marketplace** and keep `creator_level` on your candidate records. Do not build a batch that mixes levels before the quota is applied.\n3. **Bulk eligibility check.** Send up to 100 `creator_ids` to **Check Creator Outreach Eligibility** and remove anyone with `is_blocked=true`, `is_conform_to_threshold=false`, or an existing relationship you do not want to re-invite.\n4. **Bucket and cap.** Group the survivors by `creator_level`, then truncate each bucket to that level's remaining capacity (bonus first, then standard). Also apply the unchanged daily cap of 200 creators.\n5. **Send invitations by bucket.** Call **Create Target Collaboration** per bucket so that one exhausted level cannot fail an otherwise valid batch.\n6. **Handle** **`16024049` as a stop signal for that level.** Refresh the quota, mark the level as exhausted until the next Sunday, and continue with the remaining buckets.\n7. **Close the loop.** Use **Get Weekly Creator Outreach Records** (`has_sent_im_message` → `has_sent_invitation` → `is_paired`) to de-duplicate the next run and to report which levels actually convert. Bonus quota is earned from exposure-to-post performance, so wasting high-level quota on poor-fit creators reduces the seller's future capacity.\n\n### 3.2 What to change in your product surface\n| Surface | Recommended change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Quota widget | Replace the single \"remaining invitations\" number with a per-level breakdown, and show bonus separately from standard so sellers understand why one level runs out first. |\n| Creator list | Show `creator_level` as a column or tag, add a level filter, and offer an \"invitable now\" toggle driven by remaining quota plus the eligibility check. |\n| Batch builder | Warn before submission when a selection exceeds a level's remaining quota, and let the seller trim the selection instead of discovering it through errors. |\n| Error messaging | Map `16024049` to a seller-readable message: this level's weekly quota is used up, new quota arrives Sunday, other levels are still available. |\n| Scheduling | Anchor recurring outreach jobs to the Sunday refresh and spread sends across the 7-day window rather than front-loading Monday. |\n\n## 4. Timeline and action items\n| Date | What happens |\n| --- | --- |\n| Before Oct 15, 2026 | New response fields and the eligibility check API are available for integration and testing. |\n| **Oct 15, 2026** | Gradual rollout begins in the **US** market. Some shops see tiered quota first — your integration must handle both the old aggregate behavior and the new per-level behavior in the same release. |\n| After rollout | Coverage expands. Allowlisted shops move to standard tiered quota as their review completes. |\n\n**ISV action checklist**\n\n- [ ] Read and store per-level `quota_detail`, including bonus quota.\n- [ ] Persist `creator_level` on creator records from search and creator detail.\n- [ ] Call the eligibility check before every invitation batch.\n- [ ] Bucket invitations by creator level and cap each bucket by remaining quota.\n- [ ] Handle `16024049` without retry loops, and expose it to sellers in plain language.\n\n\n## 5. FAQ\n**Does this introduce a new permission scope?**\nNo. Existing Affiliate seller scopes are reused, and authorized apps do not need re-authorization.\n**Do API invitations get a separate quota?**\nNo. API, third-party tools, and Seller Center all draw on the same weekly quota for the shop.\n**Will old integrations stop working?**\nRequests keep the same shape and existing fields keep the same meaning. What changes is the outcome: invitations targeting a level with no remaining quota are rejected with `16024049` instead of succeeding.\n**How does a seller get more capacity for high-level creators?**\nBy performance. Creators who see an invitation and go on to post drive the bonus quota for higher levels, and bonus quota is consumed before standard quota.\n**Does platform-led creator matching count against quota?**\nNo, so matched collaborations should not be counted against the numbers returned by the quota API.\n",
